0,Uab Meto - Pantun - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=euufUC9gFLY,"Dec 31, 2012 · Sepriyanto Tunliu recites popular poetry in the Amanuban dialect of Uab Meto [aoz], an Austronesian language of West Timor, Indonesia.",Uab Meto,Austronesian
1,Parallel Sound Correspondences in Uab Meto - JSTOR,https://www.jstor.org/stable/43897633,"Two parallel sets of sound correspondences are attested in the historical phonology of the Uab Meto (also known as Dawan[ese], Timorese, Atoni) language/dialect cluster. A top-down approach to the data reveals one set of regular sound correspondences in reflexes of Proto-Malayo-Polynesian.",Uab Meto,Austronesian
2,"Uab Meto language. Evangelism tools, church planting ...",https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/aoz,"Audio recordings available in Uab Meto These recordings are designed for evangelism and basic Bible teaching to bring the gospel message to people who are not literate or are from oral cultures, particularly unreached people groups.",Uab Meto,Austronesian
3,Parallel Sound Correspondences in Uab Meto - ResearchGate,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/303670792_Parallel_Sound_Correspondences_in_Uab_Meto,"Jun 1, 2016 · Two parallel sets of sound correspondences are attested in the historical phonology of the Uab Meto (also known as Dawan [ese], Timorese, Atoni) language/dialect cluster.",Uab Meto,Austronesian
4,Parallel sound correspondences in Uab Meto - The Australian ...Module:Lang/data/iana languages - ChabadpediaParallel Sound Correspondences in Uab Meto,https://researchportalplus.anu.edu.au/en/publications/parallel-sound-correspondences-in-uab-meto/,"Two parallel sets of sound correspondences are attested in the historical phonology of the Uab Meto (also known as Dawan [ese], Timorese, Atoni) language/dialect cluster. Documentation for this module may be created at Module:Lang/data/iana languages/doc Two parallel sets of sound correspondences are attested in the historical phonology of the Uab Meto (also known as Dawan [ese], Timorese, Atoni) language/dialect cluster.",Uab Meto,Austronesian
5,Parallel Sound Correspondences in Uab Meto,https://openresearch-repository.anu.edu.au/items/1dfbba88-3167-42f6-a374-cb0b57c2fd76/full,"Two parallel sets of sound correspondences are attested in the historical phonology of the Uab Meto (also known as Dawan [ese], Timorese, Atoni) language/dialect cluster.",Uab Meto,Austronesian
6,Parallel Sound Correspondences in Uab Meto,https://openresearch-repository.anu.edu.au/server/api/core/bitstreams/70baaf6f-11cf-4090-bdb5-2c214e040e3e/content,"Compared to aberrant Austronesian languages, such as the Santa Cruz languages of the Solomon Islands (Ross and Næss 2007), Uab Meto is relatively “well behaved.” This comparison with MP also allows me to identify a handful of loans in Uab Meto from other MP sources.",Uab Meto,Austronesian
7,Uab Meto – TIPs,https://tips.translation.bible/tip_language/aoz/,", “become one body” in Uab Meto (source: P. Middelkoop in The Bible Translator 1952, p. 208ff. ), “tie with wife as one, so that they tie one insides” in Luang (source: Kathy and Mark Taber in Kroneman [2004], p. 539), or “become like one body-entity” (source: Tagbanwa Back Translation).",Uab Meto,Austronesian
8,(PDF) Phonology cannot transpose: evidence from Meto,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/374718250_Phonology_cannot_transpose_evidence_from_Meto,"Here, I investigate metathesis in Uab Meto (Austronesian; Indonesia), an understudied language with CV metathesis that is synchronic and productive.",Uab Meto,Austronesian
9,Low Nominative Agreement in Uab Meto,https://www.lingref.com/cpp/wccfl/39/paper3678.pdf,ways assumed to result from a ɸ-probe on T. I argue that this need not be the case; the ɸ-probe may be lower. In this paper I provide an analysis of the verbal agreement system of Uab Meto (Austronesian: Indonesia/Timor-Leste).,Uab Meto,Austronesian
